  "construction": "Symplectic-halved CPM pair-partition code: Prop. 4 of arXiv:2609.30069. (J,L,P)=(3,14,47); the CSS parent on n_par=L*P=658 qubits has block (i,l) = C(E[i][l]) over Z_47 in H_X and D[j][l] = -E[j][sigma(l)] mod 47 in H_Z, with E = [[30, 36, 39, 11, 17, 19, 15, 12, 31, 29, 32, 10, 3, 29], [33, 19, 6, 23, 1, 46, 13, 25, 9, 3, 39, 11, 3, 1], [28, 26, 43, 14, 14, 4, 32, 13, 23, 25, 1, 39, 18, 41]] and sigma(l) = l=0->7, l=1->8, l=2->12, l=3->10, l=4->13, l=5->11, l=6->9, l=7->0, l=8->1, l=9->6, l=10->3, l=11->5, l=12->2, l=13->4 (a fixed-point-free involution of the 14 block columns). The parent is folded under pi(l,t) = (sigma(l), -t) to this general stabilizer code S = (A | B) on 329 qubits; k = n - rank S.",
  "notes": "Fold of a halving-constrained draw; the CSS parent is the symplectic double and is submitted as its own entry. The exponent array solves the pair-partition equations E[i][u]-E[i][v] = -(E[j][sigma(u)]-E[j][sigma(v)]) in a null space of dimension 12 and was hill-climbed inside it, so the CSS condition and the halving identity cannot be broken by a move. k = 190 against the parent's 380. Equivalence to an existing entry was checked by the trusted gate (exact-duplicate and WL-equivalent both null). Literature novelty unverified. Distance is a witness-backed upper bound, not an exact certificate.",
